WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.400
- Is it true that you wrote
a secret song that nobody

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.280
else has ever heard and you
put it in a time capsule?

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.190
- Yes, and that has drove me crazy.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.420
- Because people bring it up?

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.950
- No, yeah, because they bring it up,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.700
but because I have written
a song that nobody's going

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.670
to hear 'til I'm 99 years
old and I might be there,

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.330
I might not be, but it's
when we did Dollywood,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.870
when reworked that, and we put
it in a time capsule to be,

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.760
you know, to be opened.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.440
- Kind of honor the opening, yeah.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.580
- And so,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.670
and I put all the things that
had to do with the times.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:37.670
I put a cassette player and
I put all the CD player.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.120
I put stuff all in this box
that if it would preserve it

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.880
to how we played those,
you know, at the time.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.140
But I put that in the box,
but I had to write this song

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.600
that nobody was going to hear 'til then.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.350
And I tell you have no idea
how that has bothered me.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.260
I wanna go dig that up so bad and think,

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.496
well, I need to use that
song 'cause it's like,

00:01:00.496 --> 00:01:02.640
you know, and it's a really good song.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.030
But, yes, I have a song that's buried

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.010
that nobody's gonna hear 'til,

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.107
I don't know whose damn idea that was.

00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:11.940
- Yeah, you're like, when is the cut-off?

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.320
Is there a date, do you know?

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.780
We need to find the date
'til we get to unearth it.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.600
- So I'm 76 and it's
when I'm 99 years old.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.890
- It is when you're 99?

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.010
- Yeah, I'd be 99 years old
when they open it, yeah.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.560
- Dolly, you got like a lot
more time to wait for that one.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.700
- I know.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.600
- But they weren't expecting
me to be there at all.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.433
- Well that's just rude.

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:33.415
- And I probably won't be.
(both laugh)

00:01:33.415 --> 00:01:34.248
- [Kelly] That's just rude.

00:01:34.248 --> 00:01:37.320
- But I mean, I'm just saying
I might be there, who knows.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.080
But the point is that
there is a song I figure

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.480
it'd probably disintegrate,
probably nobody ever hear it.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.220
That's what bothers me to think

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.010
that it's gonna be a song that
nobody's ever going to hear

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.823
if it rots in there before they open it.

00:01:49.823 --> 00:01:51.270
- But what beautiful thing
though, when they open it.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.580
What a beautiful thing.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.110
I love, I'm totally,

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.650
and I've done time capsule
gifts before, more as a joke,

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:01.050
like I gave Blake Shelton a time capsule

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.720
for his birthday last year to
open it, the one this year.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.597
And it was just like my team
Kelly jacket from The Voice.

00:02:06.597 --> 00:02:09.450
(both laugh) And I was, 'cause
he kept throwing it away,

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:12.150
and I was like, "You've had
this for a year. Joke's on you."

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.830
So, but anyway, I've
done it in a funny way

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.030
but I've never done it in a serious way.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.170
And I think that's most beautiful, too,

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.760
for like people to do for like their kids,

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.960
like make something for their kids.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.130
If you can't sing, like make a video

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.510
and like have them
unearth it at some point.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.830
I think that's really special.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.080
- Well, it'll be,
hopefully it'll be special

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.880
and hopefully you'll still be there.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.141
- Y'all enjoy it. (laughs)

00:02:29.141 --> 00:02:31.941
- Some of you might be,
some of you might not.

00:02:31.941 --> 00:02:32.774
- [Kelly] Oh my god, I love it.

00:02:32.774 --> 00:02:34.260
But it's true though, but it's not fear,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.480
I have to honestly say
it was a odd feeling

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.580
to be asked to write a
song that nobody was,

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.510
not going to hear.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.250
I mean, it was not gonna be heard.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.590
- That is annoying, it is, yeah.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.210
- But it's a good song, too.

